text:
sarah: Hey team — seeing intermittent ReadableStream hangs in a customer app running on the Vercel Edge runtime. Streams start delivering chunks, then stop mid-response and never finish. Happens ~1-2% of requests, seems latency-sensitive. Repro attached below.

kevin: Can you paste the client code and SDK version? Also any response headers when it fails?

sarah: SDK @ 0.9.2 (pinned). App uses our Node/edge build where the frontend code runs on edge functions. Repro (very small):

```ts
// simplified consumption in edge runtime
const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood-inference.local/streams', {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}` }
});
const reader = r.body?.getReader();
while (true) {
  const { value, done } = await reader!.read();
  if (done) break;
  // process chunk
}
```

kevin: Any pattern in headers? chunked encoding, transfer-encoding?

sarah: When it fails we often see Transfer-Encoding: chunked and no Content-Length. The response eventually stops emitting and the runtime never resolves `done`. If I curl the same endpoint from a normal Node runtime (not edge) it completes.

jamal: That smells like the SDK's retry/backoff or a mismatch in how the edge runtime's ReadableStream exposes the reader. In older SDKs we had a safety timeout that was removed in 1.x. Could be a retry that re-attaches and leaves a dangling reader.

emily: Do we have the customer's request id? We can trace on the proxy logs.

sarah: Yep — req-id: req_0a9f4b2c. I attached logs to the ticket. I also repro'd locally using Vercel's edge dev server and saw the same hang.

jamal: Assigning to eng-runtime for triage. @eng-runtime — can you look at how ReadableStream is implemented in the edge env vs Node? Potential suspects:
- reader.read() hang if underlying controller never calls close()/enqueue again after retry
- SDK retry logic expecting Node streams (emits 'end')

kevin: Quick triage steps for support to reproduce:
1) Use JS fetch in Vercel edge function to call our streaming endpoint.
2) Pin SDK to 0.9.2 and run load (~200 rps).
3) Observe percentage of requests that start then never finish.
4) Capture response headers and worker logs.

sarah: I also tried a quick test upgrading the SDK to 1.1.0 in a branch — saw the failure rate drop dramatically but not to zero. So looks like the newer SDK mitigates but doesn't fully fix it.

jamal: That's useful. Two parallel hypotheses: (A) earlier SDK had a retry that left the reader unresolved; (B) edge runtime polyfill for ReadableStream differs (no `'releaseLock'` semantics or different timing).

emily: Could be connection-level timeouts at Vercel ingress as well. Any 504s in the logs?

sarah: Some 504s correlated with the stall. But many stalls do NOT cause 504s — client just waits forever.

deploy-bot: deploy notice: streaming-proxy v2026.03.11 deployed to staging at 1845594300 by ci-pipeline.

jamal: Next actions I'm logging:
- eng-runtime will run targeted repro on edge runtime using SDK 0.9.2 and 1.1.0 and capture low-level stream traces (kv/timers, controller events).
- devex to add a troubleshooting doc for customers outlining: pinning suggestions, quick SDK upgrade path, and a minimal fallback (polling) if streaming stalls.
- support to collect the full HAR and worker logs for affected customers (we already have one).

kevin: For support reply to customer: ask them to try temporary patch -> upgrade SDK to 1.1.0 and enable client-side timeout (example below) while we triage server-side root cause.

```ts
// client-side safety timeout example
const reader = res.body.getReader();
const timeoutMs = 20000;
let lastChunkTs = Date.now();
setInterval(() => {
  if (Date.now() - lastChunkTs > timeoutMs) {
    // abort and surface error to app
    controller.abort();
  }
}, 5000);
```

sarah: I'll send the customer the upgrade patch and collect results. Keeping this thread updated. Thanks. :thumbsup:

jamal: Adding ticket #SUP-4821 and escalating to P2 until we confirm no server-side bug.

emily: If eng-runtime needs a quick demo environment we can provide the customer's minimal repro app (sanitized keys).

kevin: Great. Keep notes here and paste any trace IDs.

sarah: noted — will post updates.
